  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GREEN ECONOMY TRANSITION FACILITY</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Green Economic Transition Facility addresses deforestation and restoration forest (avoid desertification) and biodiversity (www.getfmw.org) and it encompasses both a matching grant component and tailored technical assistance, with its core objective centred on the provision of risk capital. The risk capital ranges from $40,000 USD to $300,000 USD. Project implementers are expected to contribute 30% of the budget through own funds or provided by financial institutions. Additionally, the GETF offers customized Technical Advisory Services, specifically tailored to address the technical aspects associated with the products, services, or technologies being introduced to the market for transitioning to clean energy sources (mitigation and adaptation).</narrative>
  </description>
